Minneapolis was home for a lot of years in a row

1306
00:44:44.400 --> 00:44:46.970
of the X games for the Summer Games.

1307
00:44:46.970 --> 00:44:50.440
She was there, you know, two years ago, 11 years old

1308
00:44:50.440 --> 00:44:53.810
and tiny and just incredibly talented.

1309
00:44:53.810 --> 00:44:56.400
And we had a really cute moment where,

1310
00:44:56.400 --> 00:44:57.700
I was babysitting this kid,

1311
00:44:57.700 --> 00:44:59.520
kinda like a nephew type kid in my life.

1312
00:44:59.520 --> 00:45:02.270
And he kind of whispered, he kind of elbowed me.

1313
00:45:02.270 --> 00:45:05.020
He's like, "there she is, that's her."

1314
00:45:05.020 --> 00:45:06.800
And I did like kind of the dorky uncle thing of like,

1315
00:45:06.800 --> 00:45:07.840
let's go meet her.

1316
00:45:07.840 --> 00:45:08.816
Yeah.

1317
00:45:08.816 --> 00:45:10.870
And like, he was mortified, but like I sat him up,

1318
00:45:10.870 --> 00:45:12.180
made him take the picture.

1319
00:45:12.180 --> 00:45:15.420
And then he has just been parading this photo ever since.

1320
00:45:15.420 --> 00:45:17.280
It's like it's his idol.

1321
00:45:17.280 --> 00:45:18.113
She's his idol.

1322
00:45:18.113 --> 00:45:20.716
It's really beautiful.
For good reason, man.

1323
00:45:20.716 --> 00:45:21.549
She is amazing.

1324
00:45:21.549 --> 00:45:22.382
Absolutely.

1325
00:45:22.382 --> 00:45:26.178
And Raimana Van Bastolaer, I think is his last name,

1326
00:45:26.178 --> 00:45:29.422
he's basically the mayor of Teahupoo

1327
00:45:29.422 --> 00:45:32.255
You know, he like is the guy there

1328
00:45:33.894 --> 00:45:36.394
and he's a Tasian surf legend,

1329
00:45:37.283 --> 00:45:39.830
and he is the head of the safety crew.

1330
00:45:39.830 --> 00:45:42.281
And so I think he must have been tapped by Kelly

1331
00:45:42.281 --> 00:45:45.500
or someone to like come and actually run.

1332
00:45:45.500 --> 00:45:46.740
So he runs the pool,

1333
00:45:46.740 --> 00:45:49.030
when he's out there, he's calling the waves,

1334
00:45:49.030 --> 00:45:51.030
he's calling positions for all the safety guys,

1335
00:45:51.030 --> 00:45:54.100
which are all great surfers in their own, right.

1336
00:45:54.100 --> 00:45:58.010
And then he's helping people like Sky get barreled,

1337
00:45:58.010 --> 00:45:59.110
figuring them out.

1338
00:45:59.110 --> 00:46:02.640
He's you know, making the pros feel comfortable.

1339
00:46:02.640 --> 00:46:04.160
They're getting what they need.

1340
00:46:04.160 --> 00:46:06.820
And then he's literally picking up likes of me and Rich

1341
00:46:06.820 --> 00:46:08.310
and making sure we get a wave.

1342
00:46:08.310 --> 00:46:11.430
And so like helping us get up and giving us tips, and-

1343
00:46:11.430 --> 00:46:12.263
My first time out,

1344
00:46:12.263 --> 00:46:15.330
he's like jump on the back of the jet ski with your board,

1345
00:46:15.330 --> 00:46:18.440
and like the complexity of the situation just went through.

1346
00:46:18.440 --> 00:46:22.470
I'm like, I'm supposed to jump off a jet ski onto the wave.

1347
00:46:22.470 --> 00:46:24.620
Like it's hard enough just to catch it for me.

1348
00:46:24.620 --> 00:46:26.430
Did you ride waves?

1349
00:46:26.430 --> 00:46:27.263
Yeah.

1350
00:46:27.263 --> 00:46:28.096
You caught some wave?

1351
00:46:28.096 --> 00:46:29.040
So they sent us all this video,

1352
00:46:29.040 --> 00:46:30.440
'cause they video, everything.

1353
00:46:30.440 --> 00:46:33.270
And it's, you know, it's like, you know,

1354
00:46:33.270 --> 00:46:35.590
a middle-aged guy riding a, you know,

1355
00:46:35.590 --> 00:46:38.392
a gigantic board and very mediocre wave.

1356
00:46:38.392 --> 00:46:39.390
And I was like, that's cool.

1357
00:46:39.390 --> 00:46:41.236
No one really needs to see that.

1358
00:46:41.236 --> 00:46:42.604
(all laughing)

1359
00:46:42.604 --> 00:46:43.683
That accidentally disappears.

1360
00:46:43.683 --> 00:46:46.593
And that's even better than what I have, but yeah.

1361
00:46:46.593 --> 00:46:48.350
I mean, I've managed it.

1362
00:46:48.350 --> 00:46:51.500
In a beautiful, kind of full circle, you know,

1363
00:46:51.500 --> 00:46:53.600
kind of reassess your life kind of way though.

1364
00:46:53.600 --> 00:46:55.752
Like, first of all, just to be invited there,

1365
00:46:55.752 --> 00:46:56.980
was incredible.

1366
00:46:56.980 --> 00:47:00.880
You can't just go there like it's, I think it's 50,000 a day

1367
00:47:00.880 --> 00:47:03.480
to rent the place and that it's usually corporate events.

1368
00:47:03.480 --> 00:47:05.570
Its booked out like years in advance.

1369
00:47:05.570 --> 00:47:07.680
It's very special to even have that experience.

1370
00:47:07.680 --> 00:47:10.550
So we were incredibly privileged to have that,

1371
00:47:10.550 --> 00:47:14.000
but Raimana goes way back with my guy,

1372
00:47:14.000 --> 00:47:18.910
Mike Field who's who is an epic Hawaii Waterman,

1373
00:47:18.910 --> 00:47:22.330
who has been my swim crew captain

1374
00:47:22.330 --> 00:47:23.850
for all of the ultramarine that I've done.

1375
00:47:23.850 --> 00:47:26.010
So every time I go to Hawaii, I hook up with him

1376
00:47:26.010 --> 00:47:28.290
and he's the guy who's guided me through those races.

1377
00:47:28.290 --> 00:47:31.580
And Mike and Raimana are super close.

1378
00:47:31.580 --> 00:47:32.640
And in addition to that,

1379
00:47:32.640 --> 00:47:35.690
another guy who was on this trip was my friend,

1380
00:47:35.690 --> 00:47:38.770
Chris Weiler, who runs a production company

1381
00:47:38.770 --> 00:47:40.340
here in LA called Dirty Robber,

1382
00:47:40.340 --> 00:47:43.890
and he does a lot of Red Bull media stuff,

1383
00:47:43.890 --> 00:47:47.670
but he was on my crew for my first ultramarine.

1384
00:47:47.670 --> 00:47:49.360
Like we're really good friends in LA.

1385
00:47:49.360 --> 00:47:52.560
So to like, and I didn't know that he was going,

1386
00:47:52.560 --> 00:47:54.260
it's like, I don't see him that often.

1387
00:47:54.260 --> 00:47:56.870
I hadn't seen him in a long time and we got to like ride

1388
00:47:56.870 --> 00:48:00.230
waves together and talk about how our lives have grown

1389
00:48:00.230 --> 00:48:03.200
and changed since that experience in 2008,

1390
00:48:03.200 --> 00:48:04.200
that changed my life.

1391
00:48:04.200 --> 00:48:05.460
And it's just really cool.

1392
00:48:05.460 --> 00:48:06.910
That's awesome.

1393
00:48:06.910 --> 00:48:10.500
And you know, to put a cap on the whole Raimana thing,

1394
00:48:10.500 --> 00:48:12.878
I just found it, his story really captivating

1395
00:48:12.878 --> 00:48:17.878
and loved hanging out with him and the Surf Ranch also,

1396
00:48:18.050 --> 00:48:20.790
what's interesting about it really is this five star

1397
00:48:20.790 --> 00:48:24.070
kind of experience, but it's in the middle of like

1398
00:48:24.070 --> 00:48:26.537
the central valley is yeah, it's in the middle.

1399
00:48:26.537 --> 00:48:29.900
It's like 45 minutes from Fresno or something like that.

1400
00:48:29.900 --> 00:48:31.520
Or 40 miles from Fresno.

1401
00:48:31.520 --> 00:48:33.010
Anybody who's driven, the five freeway

1402
00:48:33.010 --> 00:48:36.400
from LA to San Francisco knows how desolate

1403
00:48:36.400 --> 00:48:38.320
it gets in the middle of that section.

1404
00:48:38.320 --> 00:48:41.190
So imagine you're in the most desolate center

1405
00:48:41.190 --> 00:48:42.360
of that whole experience.

1406
00:48:42.360 --> 00:48:45.950
And then you exit the five freeway and then go inland,

1407
00:48:45.950 --> 00:48:49.783
you go east for another 35 minutes or so,

1408
00:48:49.783 --> 00:48:53.570
and there's nothing there except like this oasis

1409
00:48:53.570 --> 00:48:56.410
of bright...It was dark when I was driving in,

1410
00:48:56.410 --> 00:48:59.070
the night before and suddenly like in the middle

1411
00:48:59.070 --> 00:49:02.110
of like farm land, there's this huge casino.

1412
00:49:02.110 --> 00:49:05.820
And you go in there and it's the most like depressing

1413
00:49:05.820 --> 00:49:08.250
breaking bad situation you've ever seen,

1414
00:49:08.250 --> 00:49:09.470
but that's the only hotel.

1415
00:49:09.470 --> 00:49:10.900
So that's where all the surfers stay.

1416
00:49:10.900 --> 00:49:11.910
That's where everyone stays,

1417
00:49:11.910 --> 00:49:14.090
was like kind of everyone was at the bar,

1418
00:49:14.090 --> 00:49:16.070
like kind of having food and getting to know each other

1419
00:49:16.070 --> 00:49:16.970
the night before.

1420
00:49:16.970 --> 00:49:18.920
And it was just bizarre,

1421
00:49:18.920 --> 00:49:20.650
but it's like five minutes from the ranch.

1422
00:49:20.650 --> 00:49:22.480
And you go to the ranch in the morning.

1423
00:49:22.480 --> 00:49:24.640
I was reading "Pastoral Song" at that time.

1424
00:49:24.640 --> 00:49:26.830
So it's like all the breakdown of what's happened

1425
00:49:26.830 --> 00:49:29.280
in terms of industrial agriculture,

1426
00:49:29.280 --> 00:49:32.530
and you've talked about regenerative agriculture

1427
00:49:32.530 --> 00:49:33.480
on your show many times,

1428
00:49:33.480 --> 00:49:36.480
and it shows you the opposite of that like the reason

1429
00:49:36.480 --> 00:49:39.450
regenerative agriculture agriculture needs to work is that,

1430
00:49:39.450 --> 00:49:42.190
when industrial agriculture takes over an area,

1431
00:49:42.190 --> 00:49:44.770
it's bigger is the only way to succeed,

1432
00:49:44.770 --> 00:49:47.810
and so it crowds out all the people.

1433
00:49:47.810 --> 00:49:49.560
And so there's no jobs there really.

1434
00:49:49.560 --> 00:49:52.210
It's not like you don't need as many farm heads, you know,

1435
00:49:52.210 --> 00:49:55.543
it's all mechanized and the towns are crumbling.

1436
00:49:56.773 --> 00:49:58.460
I took a run around just to see it and experience it.

1437
00:49:58.460 --> 00:50:01.370
And then to go to, you know, at the time I was like,

1438
00:50:01.370 --> 00:50:03.330
why is the Surf Ranch out here?

1439
00:50:03.330 --> 00:50:05.000
But then going and experiences,

1440
00:50:05.000 --> 00:50:06.480
I'm glad the Surf Ranch is there

1441
00:50:06.480 --> 00:50:07.870
because it gives a lot of people.

1442
00:50:07.870 --> 00:50:09.950
A lot of people are having the same experience that we had

1443
00:50:09.950 --> 00:50:13.180
is like, wow, you know, there's something not working.

1444
00:50:13.180 --> 00:50:14.920
You know, like, there's something about our culture,

1445
00:50:14.920 --> 00:50:16.870
that's profoundly not working.

1446
00:50:16.870 --> 00:50:18.660
Right.
And you do see it there.

1447
00:50:18.660 --> 00:50:22.940
And so to me you could look at that,

1448
00:50:22.940 --> 00:50:23.980
maybe you don't want to see that,

1449
00:50:23.980 --> 00:50:27.070
but I actually think when you get those glimpses

1450
00:50:27.070 --> 00:50:28.560
that you're not expecting,

1451
00:50:28.560 --> 00:50:31.320
it's really could be really important.

1452
00:50:31.320 --> 00:50:34.910
And so I thought that was interesting caveat to that.

1453
00:50:34.910 --> 00:50:36.810
And then the other thing is Raimana said,

1454
00:50:36.810 --> 00:50:39.190
he surfs with all the curvatures that come through.

1455
00:50:39.190 --> 00:50:42.200
So he has surfed many times with Zuckerberg.

1456
00:50:42.200 --> 00:50:43.837
That's why we're teeing it up.

1457
00:50:43.837 --> 00:50:45.620
We're bringing it back to Zuckerberg

1458
00:50:45.620 --> 00:50:49.663
formally because Zuckerberg will rent it out for the day.

1459
00:50:51.668 --> 00:50:52.600
There's like a base nearby,

1460
00:50:52.600 --> 00:50:55.750
that's used to fly your private jet or whatever in.

1461
00:50:55.750 --> 00:50:58.847
And he comes in in the morning with his wife

1462
00:50:58.847 --> 00:51:00.520
and they just take it over for the whole day

1463
00:51:00.520 --> 00:51:01.527
and then fly back home.

1464
00:51:01.527 --> 00:51:03.800
And Raimana says, he's quite good,

1465
00:51:03.800 --> 00:51:05.280
which is really upsetting to hear.

1466
00:51:05.280 --> 00:51:06.758
I did not like it.

1467
00:51:06.758 --> 00:51:07.591
You don't want that.

1468
00:51:07.591 --> 00:51:08.424
(Adam laughing)

1469
00:51:08.424 --> 00:51:09.257
You don't want that.

1470
00:51:09.257 --> 00:51:11.390
You want this whole story about a guy dropping 50K

1471
00:51:11.390 --> 00:51:12.223
once a week.

1472
00:51:12.223 --> 00:51:13.056
And he sucks.
(Adam laughing)

1473
00:51:13.056 --> 00:51:14.070
Well, he probably wasn't good at first,

1474
00:51:14.070 --> 00:51:15.800
but if you can fly up to Surf Ranch

1475
00:51:15.800 --> 00:51:18.513
get unlimited waves for an entire day.

1476
00:51:19.890 --> 00:51:22.300
The learning curve gets shrunk considerably.

1477
00:51:22.300 --> 00:51:23.133
Welcome back, Mark.

1478
00:51:23.133 --> 00:51:23.966
How's the weekend.

1479
00:51:23.966 --> 00:51:24.980
Okay, here it is again.

1480
00:51:24.980 --> 00:51:26.570
We'll just leave it on.

1481
00:51:26.570 --> 00:51:28.777
Set it at six, have at it.

1482
00:51:28.777 --> 00:51:30.530
Yeah. And the way the wave works,

1483
00:51:30.530 --> 00:51:33.260
I mean, it is a genius feed of engineering.

1484
00:51:33.260 --> 00:51:36.680
'Cause there's literally this locomotive engine

1485
00:51:36.680 --> 00:51:41.160
that pushes this wall of water back and forth

1486
00:51:41.160 --> 00:51:42.040
and it goes back and forth.

1487
00:51:42.040 --> 00:51:45.410
So the waves go both ways, and they figured out

1488
00:51:45.410 --> 00:51:48.680
how to dissipate the water so that it calms down

1489
00:51:48.680 --> 00:51:52.480
super quickly in between waves in a way that is remarkable.

1490
00:51:52.480 --> 00:51:53.313
Oh that's cool.

1491
00:51:53.313 --> 00:51:54.910
And the wave is just unbelievable.

1492
00:51:54.910 --> 00:51:56.730
Yeah, its fast and you know,

1493
00:51:56.730 --> 00:52:01.460
we were even paddling into like the contest waves

1494
00:52:01.460 --> 00:52:06.460
at one point they had us doing, didn't you come out of there

1495
00:52:06.540 --> 00:52:07.850
with like a bruise rib.

1496
00:52:07.850 --> 00:52:11.310
I had like fin slices on both legs.

1497
00:52:11.310 --> 00:52:13.990
I had like a fractured, I still dealing with it.

1498
00:52:13.990 --> 00:52:16.150
I like cracked a rib.

1499
00:52:16.150 --> 00:52:17.297
Which I can like run and swim

1500
00:52:17.297 --> 00:52:18.570
and it doesn't really bother me.

1501
00:52:18.570 --> 00:52:20.980
But something about surfing and pushing up on the board

1502
00:52:20.980 --> 00:52:22.430
was like, yeah, it was-

1503
00:52:22.430 --> 00:52:24.680
And if you're out of the water for a while,

1504
00:52:25.560 --> 00:52:27.760
when you get back on and paddle,

1505
00:52:27.760 --> 00:52:28.593
you're gonna have those-

1506
00:52:28.593 --> 00:52:30.200
I surfed A lot in college,

1507
00:52:30.200 --> 00:52:33.013
and I literally felt like I'd never surfed in my life.

1508
00:52:33.013 --> 00:52:34.430
And then just like on a technical thing,

1509
00:52:34.430 --> 00:52:37.660
do you have any issues with the swim snorkel mask

1510
00:52:37.660 --> 00:52:38.500
while you catch away?

1511
00:52:38.500 --> 00:52:39.756
I didn't bring it.

1512
00:52:39.756 --> 00:52:40.589
Oh, no way.

1513
00:52:40.589 --> 00:52:41.422
I didn't bring it.

1514
00:52:41.422 --> 00:52:42.420
I don't know why.

1515
00:52:42.420 --> 00:52:44.010
Well, I wanted to swim in there,

1516
00:52:44.010 --> 00:52:46.145
but I didn't wanna get in the way,

1517
00:52:46.145 --> 00:52:47.360
like I wanted to be polite.

1518
00:52:47.360 --> 00:52:50.002
Like it's not about me swimming in your wave-

1519
00:52:50.002 --> 00:52:50.835
Like can you shut the waves off

1520
00:52:50.835 --> 00:52:51.668
I gotta use them some meters.

1521
00:52:51.668 --> 00:52:55.520
So, I just turned 55 and Adam gifted me

1522
00:52:55.520 --> 00:52:56.820
the best birthday gift.

1523
00:52:56.820 --> 00:52:58.773
He literally got me a snorkel mask.

1524
00:53:00.320 --> 00:53:03.040
All my efforts to get him off the mask.

1525
00:53:03.040 --> 00:53:04.300
And what does he do?

1526
00:53:04.300 --> 00:53:05.850
Just trying to get me on the mask.

1527
00:53:05.850 --> 00:53:07.760
Here we go.
(Adam laughing)

1528
00:53:07.760 --> 00:53:08.730
I mean-

1529
00:53:08.730 --> 00:53:09.563
This is happening.

1530
00:53:09.563 --> 00:53:10.950
You have to, you just have to.

1531
00:53:10.950 --> 00:53:11.783
Let me get something.

1532
00:53:11.783 --> 00:53:12.616
I have something too.

1533
00:53:12.616 --> 00:53:16.347
It's too loose right now, but you get the idea.

1534
00:53:16.347 --> 00:53:17.450
And then yeah, then you drop-

1535
00:53:17.450 --> 00:53:19.380
Your prescription lenses on this.

1536
00:53:19.380 --> 00:53:20.370
You go right to the end of the lane,

1537
00:53:20.370 --> 00:53:21.870
you drop your pool buoys, and-

1538
00:53:21.870 --> 00:53:23.980
Right. You surf with this though, right?

1539
00:53:23.980 --> 00:53:24.900
That's the idea.

1540
00:53:24.900 --> 00:53:25.733
Totally.

1541
00:53:25.733 --> 00:53:27.573
I got myself a new one.

1542
00:53:27.573 --> 00:53:28.406
Here we go.

1543
00:53:28.406 --> 00:53:31.310
Adam goes out and swims in the ocean

1544
00:53:31.310 --> 00:53:34.060
with this on rather than swimming goggles.

1545
00:53:34.060 --> 00:53:36.412
Well, I don't quite use that.

1546
00:53:36.412 --> 00:53:38.280
I got you a better one than what I used.

1547
00:53:38.280 --> 00:53:40.380
I would only use that in a dive scenario.

1548
00:53:40.380 --> 00:53:41.840
I wouldn't swim with that.

1549
00:53:41.840 --> 00:53:46.450
But if you come with us back to the brief,

1550
00:53:46.450 --> 00:53:48.600
bring that this next time, and then we can dive around.

1551
00:53:48.600 --> 00:53:50.970
You guys got iPads and glasses and goggles.

1552
00:53:50.970 --> 00:53:52.030
I'm just going shades.

1553
00:53:52.030 --> 00:53:53.500
Ah, yeah.

1554
00:53:53.500 --> 00:53:56.099
This mask is like, got its own following.

1555
00:53:56.099 --> 00:53:57.682
I got this mask.

1556
00:53:57.682 --> 00:53:58.690
It's called the devil.

1557
00:53:58.690 --> 00:53:59.540
Yeah, it's like the devil mask.

